WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:12.250
Many of you have asked us to make a video
about the Mexican elections: arguably, the

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:13.700
most important in

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:15.220
the history of Mexico, which, at the same
time it is the World’s biggest Spanish-Speaking

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:16.220
country.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:17.220
But

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:18.800
why are these so important?

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:23.160
Because this might be the first in history
where Mexico will say Goodbye to

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.500
bipartisan politics.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:32.710
Election polls: LOPEZ OBRADOR is 10.9 points
above its biggest rival

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:36.430
But wait a minute because, in fact, Mexico
was not an actual bipartisan country.

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:38.040
In fact, Mexico had the

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:41.670
same political party in the government for
over 70 years.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:43.589
Yes, you heard that right.

00:00:43.589 --> 00:00:44.589
Since 1930 until the

00:00:44.589 --> 00:00:50.299
year 2000, all the Mexican presidents belonged to the Institutional Revolutionary Party,

00:00:50.299 --> 00:00:51.299
also known as

00:00:51.299 --> 00:00:53.720
PRI for their Spanish acronym.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.909
And yes, I know what you are thinking…

00:00:55.909 --> 00:00:58.770
How can you be Revolutionary and

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:01.070
Institutional at the same time?

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:04.059
Well… nobody knows that.

00:01:04.059 --> 00:01:08.229
But this is the name they gave to this party.

00:01:08.229 --> 00:01:12.310
Theoretically, this is a center-left wing
party although many Mexicans would say they

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:13.320
are just a catch up

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:18.640
all party, with no clear ideology except by
their lust for power.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:22.979
The truth is, for 70 years, PRI was winning
every election.

00:01:22.979 --> 00:01:25.380
After the year 2000, Mexicans had a 12 years

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:30.970
hiatus of the conservative National Action
Party, also known as PAN.

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:35.130
Then, in 2012, the PRI stroke back

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:39.899
with ENRIQUE PEÑA NIETO as the president,
a guy who now holds the title of Mexico’s

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.350
most hated president

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:42.350
of all times.

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:46.859
And this is why in this very moment, 2018,
when Mexico will have this game changing elections

00:01:46.859 --> 00:01:47.859
on June the

00:01:47.859 --> 00:01:53.409
first, chances are nor the PRI, nor the PAN
will get the office.

00:01:53.409 --> 00:01:54.780
The front runner is this man you see on

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:55.780
the screen.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:57.679
His name is ANDRES MANUEL LOPEZ OBRADOR.

00:01:57.679 --> 00:02:03.119
Businessmen are worried by the LOPEZ OBRADOR
economic agenda

00:02:03.119 --> 00:02:04.939
This is the third time he runs for office.

00:02:04.939 --> 00:02:07.679
And it might the ultimate one.

00:02:07.679 --> 00:02:08.970
ANDRES MANUEL LOPEZ OBRADOR,

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:14.770
or, as Mexicans know him, AMLO, has a program
that… to put it mildly, scares the shit

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:15.770
out of business

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:17.530
people and foreign investors.

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:21.230
Some people argue that Mexico might be on
the brink of becoming the new Venezuela if

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:22.230
they choose a

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:24.100
populist politician like him.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:28.000
Nonetheless, his worst enemy is not businessmen
but himself.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.620
His testimonials are scaring away all the

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:31.640
moderate voters.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:36.840
And that is a problem because, they could
direct all this anti AMLO sentiment to one

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:37.840
of

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.220
the other candidates.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:46.410
This is why, Today’s questions are: Why
can AMLO win this election?

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:47.810
Are there real

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:50.370
reasons to be scared of him?

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:54.040
And could any other candidate really shadow
him?

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.760
Today, we are going to

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:58.820
answer all of this questions but before, let’s
take a look back at history.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:06.530
THE 
BIG MEXICAN DISSAPOINTMENT

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:11.820
At the beginning of the 21st Century, it seemed
that Mexico was taking no prisoners.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:12.820
With plenty of

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:18.900
natural resources like oil and silver, Mexican
was one of the most appreciated emerging economies.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:19.900
In

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:24.110
2010, the country’s GDP grew at a 5.5% growing
rate.

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:26.340
Nonetheless, just like the other emerging
economies

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:28.570
like Brazil or South Africa…

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:35.870
Mexico went from hero to zero in 2016.

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:40.040
Mexican GDP in dollars is on it’s worst
level since 2010

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:44.150
This is surprising if we take to account that
Mexico has all the opportunities to become

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:45.150
rich.

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:46.150
They have

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:49.460
oil, good climate for agriculture and all
kinds of natural resources.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:52.940
And what it’s more important: they

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:53.940
border with America.

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:59.730
As you know, NAFTA is a trade agreement between
Mexico, USA and Canada.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:00.730
And 80% of

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:03.320
Mexican exports go to Uncle Sam.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:09.860
Despite all of this, Mexico is still a medium
income country, with low wages and a much

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:10.860
more lower life

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:11.940
quality than its Northern Neighbours.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:16.120
And do you wonder why?

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:19.890
Well… after 70 years of a, virtually, one

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:25.939
party system, corruption and drug trafficking,
Mexico had almost medieval institutions.

00:04:25.939 --> 00:04:31.621
Oh yes, I know what you are gonna say now
‘Come on, Simon, aren’t you exhagerating

00:04:31.621 --> 00:04:32.621
a big?’

00:04:32.621 --> 00:04:33.621
Well, judge by

00:04:33.621 --> 00:04:34.621
yourself.

00:04:34.621 --> 00:04:37.650
‘Til the year 2016, their judicial system
had no presumption of innocence so it was

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:38.650
enough to

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:40.449
have a judge collecting proofs to find somebody
guilty.

00:04:40.449 --> 00:04:43.919
In many cases, a confession taken with torture

00:04:43.919 --> 00:04:46.819
would be more than enough to send somebody
to jail.

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:48.340
Imagine how would this be, that the academia
experts

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:51.229
called this system the ‘inquisitorial judicial
system’.

00:04:51.229 --> 00:04:54.690
Add to this the drug trafficking, that has
already killed more than 200 000 people…

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:57.530
in just 11 years!

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:58.680
For

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:05.550
a better understanding, in some areas of Mexico,
narcos have more power than the state itself.

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:06.550
In

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:07.740
political science, this is called a ‘failed
estate’ situation.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.319
And this happens in many areas of Africa…

00:05:10.319 --> 00:05:11.319
and in Mexico.

00:05:11.319 --> 00:05:12.319
In other words…

00:05:12.319 --> 00:05:13.889
Mexico needed more than reforms.

00:05:13.889 --> 00:05:15.949
They needed a 1803 shift on their institutions.

00:05:15.949 --> 00:05:16.949
And who

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:21.250
was the man for this job?

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:27.490
Of course, that would be ENRIQUE PEÑA NIETO,
when he got to office in 2012.

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:28.490
The

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:29.490
problem?

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:32.389
It is still to early for Mexicans to notice
some improvements on their day to day life

00:05:32.389 --> 00:05:33.389
after the

00:05:33.389 --> 00:05:34.389
reforms.

00:05:34.389 --> 00:05:38.199
In fact, social unrest can’t stop growing.

00:05:38.199 --> 00:05:45.169
Add to the fact that PEÑA NIETO’s worst
enemy is PEÑA NIETO himself.

00:05:45.169 --> 00:05:47.020
Few people have worked harder in

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:48.040
damaging their own credibility.

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:54.409
Basically, PEÑA NIETO has all the things
needed to hate a politician:

00:05:54.409 --> 00:05:58.750
corruption scandals, a fake PHD title and
embezzlement.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:00.699
But this was not enough!

00:06:00.699 --> 00:06:01.759
Do you remember Donald

00:06:01.759 --> 00:06:02.840
Trump’s campaign?

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:05.749
He was Messing with Mexicans every other day.

00:06:05.749 --> 00:06:08.319
As you can imagine, Mexicans are no big

00:06:08.319 --> 00:06:09.319
fans of Trump.

00:06:09.319 --> 00:06:10.319
So well…

00:06:10.319 --> 00:06:14.909
PEÑA NIETO’s brillian idea was to invite
Trump for an official visit even before

00:06:14.909 --> 00:06:21.620
he would become the president.

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:24.129
Guess what was the reaction of the Mexican
people!

00:06:24.129 --> 00:06:25.180
And how about the war

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:26.219
on drugs?

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:30.370
First he jailed EL CHAPO GUZMAN, who is the
Mexican version of PABLO ESCOBAR.

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:31.370
After that, EL

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:36.680
CHAPO escaped from jail from a tunnel that
was so good built that it was obvious he got

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:37.680
help from the

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:38.680
police.

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:44.110
In summary… unsurprisingly, PEÑA NIETO
is the man you love to hate.

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:51.800
A Survey in Mexico: PEÑA NIETO is the Mexican
president with the worst acceptance of all

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:52.800
times.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:57.729
In other words, PEÑA NIETO and his Administration
epitomizes the ultimate disappointment with

00:06:57.729 --> 00:06:58.729
Mexican

00:06:58.729 --> 00:06:59.729
ruling class.

00:06:59.729 --> 00:07:05.290
So PRI is not to be trusted, PAN is not very
exciting either… traditional candidates

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:06.290
are

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:07.419
not a real option anymore.

00:07:07.419 --> 00:07:09.160
So what is left?

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:13.090
Well, this is the time… for AMLO!

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:15.249
WHO IS AMLO?

00:07:15.249 --> 00:07:18.889
There was a time where AMLO was a member of
the PRI party.

00:07:18.889 --> 00:07:20.290
That was in the 70s.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:21.290
But… look, this

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:25.819
Institutional Revolutionary Party was already
more Institutional than Revolutionary.

00:07:25.819 --> 00:07:27.729
This is why AMLO

00:07:27.729 --> 00:07:32.509
left them and created another party of his
own: the Democratic Revolutionary Party, the

00:07:32.509 --> 00:07:33.509
stronghold of the

00:07:33.509 --> 00:07:35.099
true Mexican left.

00:07:35.099 --> 00:07:40.830
But… as you can imagine, defeating PRI was
mission impossible… until the year 2000.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:42.169
That year was the big

00:07:42.169 --> 00:07:44.509
crash of the biggest Mexican party.

00:07:44.509 --> 00:07:47.069
In one hand, they lost the presidency to the
conservatives.

00:07:47.069 --> 00:07:48.189
On the

00:07:48.189 --> 00:07:54.729
other, they lost the Major of the City of
Mexico to AMLO.

00:07:54.729 --> 00:08:00.800
Becoming the major of the biggest metropoli
in all across South America is not a small

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:01.800
deal.

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:02.800
You get a

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:03.800
great showcase for your policies.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:07.339
And this is why, 6 years alter, AMLO almost
won the presidency of the

00:08:07.339 --> 00:08:08.339
country.

00:08:08.339 --> 00:08:11.870
And what do you do when you “almost” win
an national election… and you are the new

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:13.919
left wing rockstar?

00:08:13.919 --> 00:08:18.400
You accuse the Government of election fraud,
organize lots of demonstrations on the streets

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:19.400
and you let

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:20.840
your followers name you the “legitimate”
president.

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:24.389
And all of this could happen once again…
if he almost wins this time.

00:08:24.389 --> 00:08:28.189
‘Clearly, this elections were unfair and
full of irregularities’

00:08:28.189 --> 00:08:31.810
‘I said in democracy you can win and you
can loose.

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:50.800
But that was not a democracy’
But now that we know his history, let’s

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.660
have a look at his policies.

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:54.880
Basically, AMLO wants to undo all

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:57.529
the reforms made by the previous presidents.

00:08:57.529 --> 00:08:59.130
Do you want examples?

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:00.500
Here we have the energy bill.

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:02.769
Prior to this law, all the Mexican oil was
managed by

00:09:02.769 --> 00:09:04.990
the state owned company, PEMEX.

00:09:04.990 --> 00:09:08.670
This company had big losts and all kinds of
corruption cases.

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:09.830
Peña Nieto

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:13.970
and his energy bill wanted to end this monopoly
so foreign companies could invest in the country.

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:14.970
As a

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:18.870
result, short term wise, gasoline prices went
sky high in some months.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:26.019
This is why, AMLO wants to go back

00:09:26.019 --> 00:09:29.460
to the previous situation, thinking that this
would solve the problem.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:31.259
The same goes with the Education bill.

00:09:31.259 --> 00:09:34.910
Prior to this one, teacher unions have a big
sway on the public

00:09:34.910 --> 00:09:35.910
education.

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:36.910
Peña Nieto changed this.

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:39.139
The result was lots of protests organized
by those teachers unions.

00:09:39.139 --> 00:09:43.660
And, again, AMLO wants to go backwards and
make those teachers happy.

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:45.199
And what about druck trafficking?

00:09:45.199 --> 00:09:46.199
Well…

00:09:46.199 --> 00:09:49.170
AMLO doesn’t stop in ending the war on drugs,
which could be kind

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:53.949
of reasonable… we wants to make an amnesty
on the big drug kingpings.

00:09:53.949 --> 00:10:00.209
‘This so-called dangerous criminals are
mere babies compared to the corrupted politicians’

00:10:00.209 --> 00:10:04.620
But the best of his policies are what we could
call the magic Tricks.

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:05.620
For example…

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:06.620
How do we end with

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:07.620
corruption?

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:08.620
Very easy!

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:10.480
You just nead to write a so-called ‘Moral
constitution’ and remove the legal

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:13.899
immunity that now enjoy the members of the
parliament.

00:10:13.899 --> 00:10:17.769
This one is specially funny because this is
not the first time that we see a polician

00:10:17.769 --> 00:10:19.170
connecting this two

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:21.600
principles: corruption and legal immunity.

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:22.600
And guess what?

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:24.520
The least corrupted countries in the planet:

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:29.060
Denmark and New Zealand HAVE legal immunity
to their member of the parliament.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:30.151
Then again, it seems like

00:10:30.151 --> 00:10:35.860
a very appealing policy for populists politicians
worldwide.

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:42.410
Anyway, AMLO seems to have easy and quick
solutions for everything.

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:44.009
Young unemployment?

00:10:44.009 --> 00:10:45.009
Easy!

00:10:45.009 --> 00:10:46.009
The

00:10:46.009 --> 00:10:47.710
govermnent will employ thousands of youngsters.

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:49.240
And so on, so forth.

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:51.040
In other words…

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:56.300
AMLO and his brand new political party, the
so called, MORENA, generate a lot of sympathy

00:10:56.300 --> 00:11:00.850
in half of the Mexican society… and a lot
of fea ron the other one.

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:04.720
And this is a problem because, if you wanna
run for office, scaring your enemies might

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.040
galvanize them on

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:07.040
the election day.

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:18.079
So the real question now is… to what extent
is AMLO willing to moderate his agenda?

00:11:18.079 --> 00:11:19.709
POPULAR OR POPULIST?

00:11:19.709 --> 00:11:21.240
Remember this name: ALFONSO ROMO.

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:25.170
He is a big businessman in MONTERREY and he
has been hired by AMLO to

00:11:25.170 --> 00:11:27.610
become the campaign’s spokesperson.

00:11:27.610 --> 00:11:28.610
What is his mission here?

00:11:28.610 --> 00:11:30.860
Well… he is the man in charge of moderating

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:34.520
AMLO’s policies and make them more palatable
for the independent voters.

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:39.089
Having all the polls on his favour, AMLO needs
those votes badly.

00:11:39.089 --> 00:11:40.630
And ALFONSO ROMO is the man for the

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:41.630
job.

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:45.230
He comes from the business world and he used
to support conservative candidates in the

00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:46.230
past.

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:47.230
In

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:49.810
fact, many of AMLO’s advisors come from
different backgrounds, including the conservative

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:51.220
PAN party.

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:52.220
And

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:54.170
you can tell they are really softening AMLO’s
rethoric.

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:59.569
Do you remember I told you that AMLO wanted
to revoke the energy bill?

00:11:59.569 --> 00:12:01.069
Well, now Alfonso Romo has said

00:12:01.069 --> 00:12:03.250
that… ‘look guys, this was not so bad.

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:06.500
At the end of the day, we will just renegociate
the contracts with

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:09.899
foreign companies but they can stay in the
country, right?

00:12:09.899 --> 00:12:11.569
We really looooove business.

00:12:11.569 --> 00:12:12.569
Really!’

00:12:12.569 --> 00:12:17.209
AMLO changed his mind and now he sais yes
to energy openness… according to Alfonso

00:12:17.209 --> 00:12:18.209
Romo

00:12:18.209 --> 00:12:20.269
But there is still a lot more last minute
moderation!

00:12:20.269 --> 00:12:22.570
Look, AMLO is from a region called TABASCO.

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:23.570
And

00:12:23.570 --> 00:12:25.129
there, there is a famous kind of fish called
PEJE *PRONOUNCED LIKE ‘PECHE’ IN CZECH*.

00:12:25.129 --> 00:12:26.129
This is why, some

00:12:26.129 --> 00:12:27.139
people nickname him as THE PEJE.

00:12:27.139 --> 00:12:30.470
So now, in order to give the impression that
he will not nationalize

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:34.730
companies, nor rise taxes or expropriate properties
on a Venezuelan fashion, he has launched a

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:35.730
brand new

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:36.730
economic agenda called…

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:37.730
PEJENOMICS.

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:38.730
Isn’t it a catchy title?

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:44.370
But… as you know money is no big fan of
risks and experiments.

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:46.400
And, with or without flashy names and

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:48.540
mixed signals, the Mexican businessmen don’t
really trust AMLO.

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:50.100
This is why, while elections are getting

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:54.879
closer and closer, Mexican inteligentia has
already found their candidate.

00:12:54.879 --> 00:12:57.709
Don’t forget that Mexico,

00:12:57.709 --> 00:13:02.270
unlike other countries like France, has no
second round on the presidential elections.

00:13:02.270 --> 00:13:03.270
This means that,

00:13:03.270 --> 00:13:08.110
the one with the biggest share of voters on
July the 1st will become the president.

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:09.110
This is why, it seems

00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:13.019
that the big antagonist to AMLO is going to
be this the conservative candidate, whose

00:13:13.019 --> 00:13:14.019
name is RICARDO

00:13:14.019 --> 00:13:15.839
ANAYA.

00:13:15.839 --> 00:13:21.959
The Mexican business elite will support ANAYA
in order to stop LOPEZ OBRADOR

00:13:21.959 --> 00:13:25.500
Being 39 years old, ANAYA is the youngest
candidate on this elections.

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:26.870
He is been accused of money

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:27.870
laundering.

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:29.709
But, despite what it looks, this hasn’t
hurt him during the campaign.

00:13:29.709 --> 00:13:31.070
In fact, the opposite

00:13:31.070 --> 00:13:32.070
is true.

00:13:32.070 --> 00:13:35.779
People believe that this was just a dirty
deed from the PRI to disqualify him.

00:13:35.779 --> 00:13:36.779
So he is gaining

00:13:36.779 --> 00:13:43.920
momentum on the polls… although, he still
has a long way to surpass AMLO.

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:44.920
SO now the big question is…

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:48.620
Do you believe AMLO will become the next Mexican
president or maybe ANAYA

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:50.100
will challenge him?

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:54.600
Is AMLO a risk for Mexico or… it is hard
to do worse than the previous presidents?

